// A `never()` binding in two arrays, read through a block as a number:
// the arrays' element cells were fixed without it and each then asked its
// own type of it, "a value here is used as i64 and as Array<i64>", where
// the same program without the block checks (soak nov24f, block-wrap and
// let-inline flips).
// Expected trace (both engines): 0.
{ let x = never(); let a = ([x, [x, 1]], 2 - { let t = x; t }); 0 }
